        <mxCell id="c84" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the three families whose decision is to buy only with the crew reduced. A positive effect means buying saves money; with the crew kept (column M) every quoted family costs money to buy, and the CFO&#x27;s absorption view (column L) is positive for five of the six. Columns B to F, H, K and P to Z are hidden here, and the columns are narrower than the workbook&#x27;s; the formula bar shows the rule of the decision cells, which also asks (column Y) whether the two years the quote is fixed cover the family&#x27;s one-time costs.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="365" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
